{
	"version": 5,
	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "tOls6SnVqoxCuVv-y",
			"name": "Fleshborer",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The most common weapon in the swarm: a fused, fleshy launcher that fires a swarm of ravenous, flesh-eating beetles at the target, where they burrow in and devour tissue from the inside. Codex: Tyranids background across editions treats the Fleshborer as the baseline Termagant/Hormagaunt-carried gun, present in overwhelming numbers rather than individually deadly — what makes a gaunt brood dangerous is weight of fire, not any one shot's punch.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor (updated after flak went to DR 30, replacing an earlier 6d pi+ that left a Termagant brood unable to hurt a flak-armoured Guardsman at all — 0.99% per hit): \"Fleshborer | Fires burrowing beetles: 6d(2) pi+.\" Innate Attack (Large Pierce) (B61, 6/die) at 6 dice = 36, with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%): 36x1.5=54. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6d(2) pi+ averages 21 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 90.4% of the time, and rounds to 0% against carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) or anything heavier — now a real threat to flak, per the anchor's own \"kills unarmoured men, struggles against carapace\" wording, while carapace (and everything above it) remains untouched, exactly the gap the divisor correction exists to fix. Handling: Acc 2 (an organic launcher with no sights, between an Ork shoota's crude 1-2 and a proper Imperial rifle's 4-5, since a Tyranid's own instinct aims better than a Boy's guesswork even without optics) and range 80/240 (the anchor's own \"short range,\" read as roughly submachine-gun reach) are this project's own estimate, since no anchor gives exact figures; Shots 6(60), a one-minute brood-regrowth, reflects the symbiote's living ammunition rather than a magazine.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 54,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "W-_A32QsjZN6bKwkr",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "pi+",
						"base": "6d",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"accuracy": "2",
					"range": "80/240",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "6(60)",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "ST-independent: grown fused to the bearer's arm, not carried, so any Termagant or Hormagaunt fires it at full effect regardless of its own ST. Shots regrow: the beetle brood living in the weapon's bio-mass regenerates over the listed time rather than being reloaded; a Fleshborer that has just emptied its brood is out of the fight for about a minute, not permanently disarmed.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Innate Attack"
							},
