							"modifier": -4
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tC6rzISzBlLGVExGG",
			"name": "Spinefists",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A pair of chitinous launchers, one on each forearm, that spray a hail of stiff, needle-like bio-spines — a swarm weapon built to saturate a target with volume rather than land one telling hit, carried by Hormagaunts and lesser gaunt broods that close fast and shoot on the move. Codex: Tyranids background consistently frames Spinefists as a \"spray and pray\" weapon rather than a precision one.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor (updated after flak went to DR 30, for the same reason as the Fleshborer above): \"Spinefists | 3d(2) pi+ spines, RoF 6.\" Innate Attack (Large Pierce) (B61, 6/die) at 3 dice = 18, with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%) and Rapid Fire (B105, RoF 5-8 bracket, +70%): net +120%, 18x2.2=39.6, rounded to 40. Checked by exact dice distribution: 3d(2) pi+ averages 10.5 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 4.6% of the time per spine, and rounds to 0% against carapace (DR 70) or anything heavier — still a weak single hit, exactly the \"sprays a swarm of weak hits\" role the anchor's own low dice count implies; the weapon's actual threat at the table comes from RoF 6 giving several rolls to fish for an unarmoured hit, a Weak Points chink, or now an occasional flak penetration, not from any one spine's own punch. Handling: Acc 1 (a spray weapon, the lowest bracket this project uses, matching an Ork shoota's own crude accuracy for the same reason: volume over precision) and a short 60/180 range, both this project's own estimate for a close-assault arm-launcher. Shots 20(30), a half-minute regrowth for the lighter, faster-cycling spine-glands.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 40,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WpIH4VtSV1lBCEegT",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
