		{
			"id": "tb0w9EDSsHtuyRww5",
			"name": "Deathspitter",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A rifle-class gun-arm that spits a single, heavy globule of acid maggots in place of the Devourer's rapid worm-stream: a slower, much harder-hitting bio-weapon carried by Tyranid Warriors who need to bring down an armoured target rather than saturate a firing line. Codex: Tyranids background and Deathwatch RPG bio-weapon material both treat it as the swarm's answer to a rifle-class corrosive weapon, genuinely dangerous to carapace and a real if inconsistent threat to power armour.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Deathspitter | Acid maggots: 6d×2(2) cor.\" Innate Attack (Corrosion) (B61, 10/die) at an effective 12 dice (6 base dice x2 multiplier, priced per this file's header convention) = 120, with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%): 120x1.5=180. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx2(2) cor averages 42 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 99.98%, carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) 79.4%, Sororitas plate (DR 85, eff. 42.5) 45.4%, Astartes plate (DR 100, eff. 50) 14.5%, and rounds to 0% against a Terminator — a real, reliable threat to carapace and a genuine if inconsistent one to power armour, matching the anchor's own implied step up from the Devourer. Handling: Acc 4 and 150/450 range, this project's own rifle-class estimate matching the Devourer's own range at a slower cycle; Shots 8(30), fewer but bigger globules per regrowth than the Devourer's worm-stream.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 180,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WR4l3KE_lcF-DxzAR",
