		{
			"id": "tYg9hGC_RBwpPfKGT",
			"name": "Venom Cannon",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavy bio-cannon that hurls a dense, explosive mass of caustic bile at a single target hard enough to crack light armour outright — the swarm's first real answer to armoured infantry and light vehicles, most often seen mounted on Tyranid Warriors and Carnifexes. Codex: Tyranids background across editions and Deathwatch RPG material both describe it as capable of blowing an unarmoured target apart and staggering even power-armoured targets with a solid hit.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Venom cannon | 6d×3(3) cr ex.\" Innate Attack (Crush) (B61, 5/die) at an effective 18 dice (6 base x3 multiplier) = 90, with Explosion (B102, +50%, for the \"ex\" bursting bile) and Armor Divisor (3) (B102, +100%): net +150%, 90x2.5=225. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx3(3) averages 63 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 10) 100%, carapace (DR 70, eff. 23.3) 100%, Sororitas plate (DR 85, eff. 28.3) 99.8%, Astartes plate (DR 100, eff. 33.3) 99.0%, and Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 66.7) 36.3% — genuinely \"cracks armour,\" including a real chance against Terminator-grade plate. Against vehicles: AV10 99.0%, AV11 85.5%, AV12 36.3%, AV13 0.99%, AV14 0% — a real light-vehicle killer, no threat at all to a main battle tank, exactly the light-anti-armour niche the anchor implies without inflating it into a lascannon. Handling: Acc 4 and 200/600 range, this project's own heavy-symbiote estimate; Shots 4(60), a one-minute regrowth for the biggest single discharge in the venom-gland family.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 225,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "Wfy6y8Axa-yUtfsOG",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "6dx3",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"accuracy": "4",
					"range": "200/600",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "4(60)",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "ST-independent, grown as a torso- or arm-mounted organ (Tyranid Warrior/Carnifex-scale bioforms only). Shots regrow over the listed time as the bearer's bile-gland refills.",
