		{
			"id": "tpCz8cjyRtXpTMBYy",
			"name": "Barbed Strangler",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Fires a bulbous seed pod that bursts on impact into a tangle of whipping, barbed vines, tearing at everyone nearby rather than punching through one target's armour — an area-denial weapon rather than an armour-cracker, most often carried by Tyranid Warriors screening a swarm's advance. Codex: Tyranids background describes it explicitly as an anti-infantry, area-covering weapon distinct from the venom cannon's single-target punch.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Barbed strangler | Seed pod that grows barbed vines: 4d cr ex [3d cut] area.\" Innate Attack (Crush) (B61, 5/die) at 4 dice = 20, with Explosion (B102, +50%), Area Effect (B102, +50%, 2-yard radius) and Fragmentation (B105; no exact published percentage covers \"spawns a separate cutting attack across the same radius,\" so this project prices it at an estimated +20%, by the same \"eyeball a documented departure\" practice this project uses elsewhere for un-tabled Basic Set options): net +120%, 20x2.2=44. Checked by exact dice distribution: both the 4d cr ex primary and the 3d cut vine-burst round to 0% against flak (DR 30) or anything heavier — correctly weak against any real armour, since the anchor's whole point is area coverage against unarmoured or lightly-armoured infantry, not penetration. Handling: Acc 3 and a shorter 100/300 range (a lobbed pod, not a direct-fire cannon), this project's own estimate; Shots 3(120), a two-minute regrowth for the biggest single pod in the gland.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 44,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "Wy2PmYlcP20qGSKEA",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr ex",
						"base": "4d"
					},
					"accuracy": "3",
					"range": "100/300",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "3(120)",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Area Effect, 2-yard radius (B102): everyone in the burst radius, not only the hit target, takes 3d cut as the pod's barbed vines burst outward and lash the area — resolve as a single Innate Attack roll against the primary target, then 3d cut to everyone else caught in the radius, per this project's follow-up convention. ST-independent, grown as a torso-mounted organ. Shots regrow over the listed time.",
