		{
			"id": "thJ_G3R78Ym03NVGH",
			"name": "Heavy Venom Cannon",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Carnifex's own up-gunned venom cannon: the same bursting-bile mechanism as the standard weapon, grown far larger in a bioform built as a living battering ram. Codex: Tyranids background treats the Carnifex's cannon as a genuine tank-and-Terminator threat where a Warrior's own venom cannon is only a light-vehicle killer, matching the Carnifex's role as the swarm's dedicated heavy-support beast.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this pattern by dice; it is built one size class above the Venom Cannon the same way this project's own Necron Gauss Cannon steps up from the Gauss Blaster: the Venom Cannon's dice pushed one multiplier step further (6dx3 to 6dx4) at the same divisor. Innate Attack (Crush) (B61, 5/die) at an effective 24 dice (6 base x4 multiplier) = 120, with Explosion (+50%) and Armor Divisor (3) (+100%): net +150%, 120x2.5=300. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx4(3) averages 84 and clears every personal-armour DR at 99.9%+, including a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 66.7) at 85.5%. Against vehicles: AV10 99.9%, AV11 98.0%, AV12 85.5%, AV13 36.3%, AV14 2.0% — a genuine tank-and-Terminator threat at the light-to-medium end, dropping off hard against a Leman Russ or Land Raider's own frontal glacis, exactly matching \"cracks tanks and Terminators, doesn't reliably crack the very heaviest armour\" for a Carnifex-scale weapon rather than a dedicated lascannon-class one. Handling: Acc 4 and 250/750 range, one step past the standard Venom Cannon; Shots 3(90), fewer shots and a shorter regrowth than the lighter weapon for the much bigger single discharge.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 300,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "Wv6aJYps1MsM0hSoq",
					"sv": 1,
