		{
			"id": "tB4k9c9KFlNSgIqPS",
			"name": "Stranglethorn Cannon",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Tyrannofex's own bio-titan-scale strangler gland: the same barbed-vine-pod mechanism as the standard Barbed Strangler, grown to a size that saturates a much wider killing ground rather than hitting any harder against real armour. Codex: Tyranids background is explicit that the Tyrannofex's strangler arm is an anti-infantry area weapon, not the anti-tank one — that job belongs to its other, rupture-cannon arm, which this project does not build here since it is a fixed-effect weapon this file's Innate Attack build cannot honestly represent without inventing new mechanics.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this pattern; built one size class above the Barbed Strangler the same relationship the Heavy Venom Cannon uses over the standard Venom Cannon: dice doubled (4d to 6dx2), radius doubled (2 to 4 yards), divisor left at (1) since the anchor's own Barbed Strangler has none either — this is an area-saturation weapon, not an armour-cracker, and giving it a divisor would misrepresent its actual battlefield role. Innate Attack (Crush) (B61, 5/die) at an effective 12 dice (6 base x2 multiplier) = 60, with Explosion (+50%), Area Effect (+50%, 4-yard radius) and the same estimated Fragmentation +20% the Barbed Strangler uses: net +120%, 60x2.2=132. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx2 cr ex averages 42 and penetrates flak (DR 30) 90.4% of the time but rounds to 0% against carapace (DR 70) or anything heavier, and 0% against every vehicle DR in the table — a real killer of unarmoured and lightly-armoured infantry over a wide area, and honestly no threat at all to real armour, exactly matching the anchor's own division of labour between the strangler (area, anti-infantry) and rupture cannon (anti-tank) arms. Handling: Acc 3 and 150/450 range (a lobbed, area-covering weapon, not a direct-fire cannon, so range is kept modest despite the bioform's huge size); Shots 3(120), matching the standard strangler's own figures at bio-titan scale.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 132,
