		{
			"id": "tyAIxdWE29zZ4RvPa",
			"name": "Bio-plasma",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A bio-cannon that spits a searing, self-sustaining ball of superheated bile — the Carnifex's answer to an Imperial plasma weapon, grown rather than engineered, and just as capable of punching through power armour. Codex: Tyranids background across editions singles out bio-plasma as one of the most dangerous ranged weapons a Carnifex can be grown to carry, a real threat to Terminator-grade plate rather than merely power armour.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this weapon by dice, only by role (\"a Carnifex spit\" capable of matching Imperial plasma per this project's brief); it is built directly on framework.md's own Plasma Gun anchor (6d×4(3) burn ex) rather than a re-derived figure, the same judgement this project's Necron Particle Beamer entry makes against the same anchor, since bio-plasma's fictional role — kills Marines through power armour, a real if inconsistent threat to Terminators — is identical to plasma's own. Innate Attack (Burn) (B61, 5/die) at an effective 24 dice (6 base x4 multiplier) = 120, with Explosion (+50%) and Armor Divisor (3) (+100%): net +150%, 120x2.5=300 — identical cost math to the Heavy Venom Cannon above, since both use the same 5-point-per-die type rate and the same modifier stack; only the damage type (burn vs. crush) differs. Checked by exact dice distribution (identical to the Heavy Venom Cannon's own figures, since the dice and divisor match): clears every personal-armour DR at 99.9%+, Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 66.7) at 85.5%, and the vehicle table at 2.0%-99.9% across AV10-14 — a genuine, reliable threat to power armour and a real (if not overwhelming) one to Terminator plate, exactly matching bio-plasma's fictional reputation. Handling: Acc 3 and 150/450 range, shorter than the Heavy Venom Cannon's own reach since a spat globule of bile doesn't fly as flat or as far as a solid mass; Shots 3(90), matching the Heavy Venom Cannon's own regrowth figures for a comparably huge single organ.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 300,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WfPjkVMxrVAWhcojt",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "burn ex",
						"base": "6dx4",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"accuracy": "3",
					"range": "150/450",
					"rate_of_fire": "1",
					"shots": "3(90)",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "ST-independent; grown only on Carnifex-scale bioforms. No overheat risk: unlike an Imperial plasma weapon's unstable containment coil, this is a living organ regulating its own reaction, so it never has a Malfunction roll for the discharge itself. Shots regrow over the listed time.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Innate Attack"
							},
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Projectile"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tOmXCuCURbajG8Je-",
			"name": "Scything Talons",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A pair of long, chitinous cutting blades grown from the forearms — the single most common melee symbiote in the swarm, carried by everything from Genestealers to Hive Tyrants in one form or another. Codex: Tyranids background across editions treats scything talons as the baseline killing weapon: not the swarm's hardest-hitting blade, but reliable, always-on, and lethal against anything short of the heaviest personal armour.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Scything talons | sw+2d(2) cut.\" Built at a Tyranid Warrior's own ST 34 (sw 6d, framework's bioform table): Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%) = 7x1.5=10.5, rounded to 11, for the bare sw+0(2) cut baseline the wielder's own ST already provides for free; the anchor's own +2d on top is bought separately as Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 2 dice = 14, with Armor Divisor (2) (+50%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (B112, -30%): net +20%, 14x1.2=16.8, rounded to 17. Total 11+17=28. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 34 (sw+2d(2) = 8d(2)): averages 28 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 99.6% of the time, carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) 6.1%, and rounds to 0% against Astartes plate (eff. 50) and Terminators — a real killer of unarmoured and flak-armoured targets and only a marginal threat to carapace and none to rigid plate, matching \"lethal against anything short of the heaviest personal armour\" without overstating it against carapace. (A Ravener at ST 32, 8d-1(2): flak 99.3%, carapace 3.9%.) Skill: Brawling, per framework.md's own weapon- skill table for natural close-combat weapons (power fist/lightning claws use the same skill).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 28,
