		{
			"id": "tcVy31Wk6tIy7s9Ps",
			"name": "Scything Talons (Hormagaunt)",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Hormagaunt's own scything talons: a leaping killer's blades, swung in a frenzy by a body built to close on prey and shred it. Codex: Tyranids background treats the Hormagaunt as the swarm's melee shock troop, whose whole purpose is to cut down infantry in the open; a Hormagaunt brood that cannot hurt a flak-armoured Guardsman would not be worth growing.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's Scything Talons anchor (sw+2d(2) cut) is written at a Tyranid Warrior's ST 34; at a Hormagaunt's ST 12 (sw 1d+2) it yields only 3d+2(2), which penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 16.2% of the time and leaves the swarm's leaping killer unable to reliably hurt the Guardsmen it exists to shred (weaker than a Termagant's fleshborer, 6d(2) at 90%). This entry keeps the same build with four dice of Innate Attack instead of two: Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%) = 10.5, rounded to 11, for the bare sw(2) baseline; Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 4 dice = 28, with Armor Divisor (2) (+50%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +20%, 28x1.2=33.6, rounded to 34. Total 11+34 = 45. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 12 (sw+4d(2) = 5d+2(2)): averages 19.5 and penetrates flak 84.8% of the time, carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) 0%, and nothing heavier - a real killer of unarmoured and flak-armoured infantry (a brood of them certainly is) and no threat to rigid plate.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 45,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "w4xtCWNxaL5Pl9Muj",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
