		{
			"id": "tBJJ_RDML2KDme4Zi",
			"name": "Rending Claws",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Genestealer's signature weapon: claws sharp and strong enough to punch clean through ceramite and plasteel on a solid hit, not merely cut flesh. Codex: Tyranids background and the Deathwatch RPG's own Genestealer material both single out rending claws as capable of shearing through power armour where an ordinary scything talon cannot — precisely the divisor-swap-on-a-good-hit this project's \"rending\" house rule (framework.md) exists to model.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Rending claws | sw+2d(3) cut; rending: a hit that succeeds by 5+ or is a critical uses armour divisor (10) instead.\" Built at a Genestealer's own ST 26 (sw 5d, framework's bioform table): Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (3) (B102, +100%) = 14 for the sw+0(3) baseline; the anchor's own +2d is bought as Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 2 dice = 14, with Armor Divisor (3) (+100%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +70%, 14x1.7=23.8, rounded to 24. Total 14+24=38. The Rending hit line costs nothing extra: it is the same attack, the same dice, and the same points already paid above — only the armour divisor applied to a hit that already succeeded well changes, exactly as framework.md's own rule describes it (a chance-based crit effect, not a bought capability). Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 26 (sw+2d = 7d): the ordinary (3) line averages 24.5 and penetrates flak (eff. 10) 99.96%, carapace (eff. 23.3) 58.6%, Astartes plate (eff. 33.3) 2.2%, and 0% against a Terminator (eff. 63.3) — a solid melee weapon on an ordinary hit, a fair carapace-cracker and no Marine-killer. The Rending hit's (10) line, same 7d average 24.5: flak 100%, carapace (eff. 7) 100%, Astartes plate (eff. 10) 99.96%, and even a Terminator (eff. 19) 86.3% — genuinely \"shears through ceramite,\" exactly what the anchor's own text claims, and only on the hits the rending rule says should count. (A Lictor at ST 36 has sw 6d+1, so 8d+1: ordinary line flak 100%, carapace 87.0%, Astartes plate 17.9%, Terminator 0%; Rending line Astartes plate 100%, Terminator 97.6%.)",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 38,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wRBj9zMIdllfOhVaw",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "2d",
						"armor_divisor": 3
					},
					"reach": "1",
					"parry": "0",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Rending: on a hit that succeeds by 5 or more, or on a critical hit, use the Rending hit line below instead of this one (roll the same damage dice, but apply divisor (10)) — framework.md's own rending rule, priced here as a conditional reinterpretation of an already-bought hit rather than a separately-purchased ability, since it never triggers without this weapon's own attack roll succeeding well in the first place.",
					"defaults": [
						{
