		},
		{
			"id": "tI6sK-ZFYqx4aUi8I",
			"name": "Bonesword",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A blade of psychically-hardened bone, carried by Tyranid Warriors and Primes and charged with a disruptive field the Hive Mind itself sustains — the swarm's own answer to a power weapon, shearing through armour a plain scything talon or rending claw cannot touch. Codex: Tyranids background places boneswords firmly in the same armour-shredding tier as an Astartes power sword, usually wielded alongside a Lash Whip that pins a target still for the killing blow.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Bonesword | Psychically charged bone blade: sw+3d(10) cut (power-field class).\" Built at a Tyranid Warrior's own ST 34 (sw 6d): Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (10) (B102, +200%) = 21 for the sw+0(10) baseline; the anchor's own +3d is bought as Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 3 dice = 21, with Armor Divisor (10) (+200%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +170%, 21x2.7=56.7, rounded to 57. Total 21+57=78 — priced in the same tier as this project's Custodes power weapons for the same reason: a divisor-(10) weapon is always expensive to buy as a character trait, whatever grows or forges it. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 34 (sw+3d(10) = 9d(10)): averages 31.5 and clears every personal-armour DR at 100%, including Astartes plate (DR 100, eff. 10) at 100%, and a Terminator (DR 190, eff. 19) at 99.2% — a genuine Marine-and-near-Terminator killer, matching \"same armour-shredding tier as a power sword\" (framework's own power sword anchor, sw+3d+1(10), sits almost exactly here) without exceeding it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 78,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wsb0SRzNbr9SeZjlr",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
