		{
			"id": "tGDANVDVgSsGkrRbG",
			"name": "Monstrous Crushing Claws",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A pair of massive crushing pincers grown in place of scything talons on some Carnifexes and Hive Tyrants, built to pulp armour and machinery outright rather than cut through it — the bio-weapon most often shown in Codex: Tyranids background and Black Library's Tyranid-focused fiction alike caving in a Dreadnought's hull or snapping a Rhino's axle in one blow.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Monstrous crushing claws | thr+6d(5) cr.\" Built at a Carnifex's own ST 60 (thr 7d-1): Crushing Striker (B88, 5 points) with Armor Divisor (5) (B102, +150%) = 5x2.5=12.5, rounded to 13, for the thr+0(5) baseline; the anchor's own +6d is bought as Innate Attack (Crush) (B61, 5/die) at 6 dice = 30, with Armor Divisor (5) (+150%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +120%, 30x2.2=66. Total 13+66=79. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 60 (thr+6d(5) = 13d-1(5)): averages 44.5 and clears every personal-armour DR up to and including Astartes plate at 100%, dropping to 74.0% against a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 40) — the hardest-hitting personal-scale melee weapon in this file against the very heaviest infantry armour. Against vehicles: AV10 100%, AV11 98.9%, AV12 74.0%, AV13 3.7%, AV14 0% — genuinely \"cracks a Dreadnought or a Rhino,\" matching the anchor and the fiction, while still falling short of a main battle tank's frontal glacis, which is exactly the gap between this and a true anti-tank symbiote (the Heavy Venom Cannon or Stranglethorn Cannon above).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 79,
			"weapons": [
				{
