		{
			"id": "tfaTxHsog69AAB24f",
			"name": "Flesh Hooks",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cluster of long, backward-curved hooks grown from the forearms of Raveners and some Tyranid Primes, built less to kill outright than to snag a fleeing target or drag an objective-holder out of cover and into the swarm's reach. Codex: Tyranids background and the current tabletop's own objective-control rules for Flesh Hooks agree on this grab-and-drag role over a purely offensive one.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names Flesh Hooks by dice, only by role (grapple and drag), so it is built as a plain natural weapon at a Ravener's own ST 36 (thr 4d-1; a Ravener at ST 32 has 3d+1) with no bonus dice bought on top, since its point is the grab, not the kill: Impaling Striker (B88, 8 points, the hooked-barb reading of a Piercing Striker's family) with the Long 1 enhancement (this project's own estimated +40%/level, as the Lash Whip above) for the extra reach the hooks need to snag at range 2: 8x1.4=11.2, rounded to 11. No exact-dice penetration table is given since Flesh Hooks are not built or priced as an armour-cracking weapon; thr imp at ST 36 (4d-1 imp) is a believable puncture against flesh and unarmoured targets, and the grapple note above is the symbiote's actual battlefield function.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 11,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wnskw46RnqAWkoyo0",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "imp",
						"st": "thr"
					},
					"reach": "1,2",
					"parry": "No",
