		{
			"id": "tLvwHyXofRMq9dY2M",
			"name": "Toxin Sacs",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Venom glands laced through a bioform's claws or fangs, so that any solid melee hit also injects a fast-acting neurotoxin on top of whatever the blade or claw itself did — a common upgrade on Genestealers and Tyranid Warriors whose base melee symbiote might not finish an armoured target outright. Codex: Tyranids background is explicit that Tyranid toxins are potent enough to drop a human in a single dose and give even an Astartes' superhuman physiology real trouble.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Toxic) (B61, 4/die) at 2 dice = 8, with Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): 8x0.7=5.6, rounded to 6. Bought as a Follow-Up (B105) to whichever melee symbiote the bearer already carries — per Basic Set's own rule, Follow-Up carries no separate cost modifier of its own, since the restriction (it can only trigger when the carrier attack lands) is already priced into the low, flat dice count here rather than into a percentage. Framework.md's own follow-up convention (B414: follow-up damage applies only once the carrier attack has itself penetrated the target's DR) is used as written: a Toxin Sacs hit only matters once the accompanying claw or fang has already got through armour, so it adds real danger against anything the bearer can already wound, and nothing at all against anything it can't.",
