		{
			"id": "tJ7X0TpkJ8pqsx2AP",
			"name": "Adrenal Glands",
			"reference": "B17",
			"local_notes": "Basic Speed +0.5; Striking ST +2 (thrust/swing damage only).\n\nLore: A cluster of hormonal glands wired directly into a Tyranid's nervous system, keeping it primed for violence at all times rather than needing a fight-or-flight trigger the way a human's own adrenaline does — Codex: Tyranids background across editions describes Adrenal Glands as a straightforward, always-on upgrade that makes a bioform faster and hits harder in melee, common on Genestealers, Warriors and Hive Tyrants alike.\n\nDesign: Increased Basic Speed +0.50 (B17, 5 points per 0.25 level, 10 points), matching this project's own Ork Warboss precedent for the same advantage, plus Striking ST +2 (B88, 5 points/level, 10 points) for the extra melee punch. 20 points total. Built as a flat, always-on trait rather than a conditional/triggered bonus (contrast this project's Ork WAAAGH! Gestalt or Warpath, which are explicitly situational): the fiction shows Adrenal Glands working continuously rather than switching on under threat, matching a species whose whole biology the Hive Mind keeps at a permanent combat pitch.",
