			]
		},
		{
			"id": "ttKpextNgyKz8JTZd",
			"name": "Acid Maw",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A gaping maw ringed with dissolving digestive acid rather than ordinary teeth, carried by the biggest burrowing terrors of the swarm — Trygons and Mawlocs erupting from the earth to close their jaws on a Rhino or a squad of Guardsmen alike. Codex: Tyranids background and Black Library's Tyranid-focused fiction (widely depicted; no single canonical figure for this specific bite) both show an Acid Maw shearing through light vehicle armour as readily as flesh.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor names this weapon; it is built one size class above the Deathspitter's own corrosive-acid family (the same \"maggots vs. digestive acid\" mechanism, scaled to a bio-titan's own bite rather than a Warrior's gun-arm) and fixed rather than sw/thr- based, since Trygons and Mawlocs sit above framework.md's own bioform table and inventing an ST figure for them would be a bigger, unstated departure than pricing the bite directly. Innate Attack (Corrosion) (B61, 10/die) at an effective 18 dice (6 base x3 multiplier) = 180, with Armor Divisor (3) (+100%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +70%, 180x1.7=306. Checked by exact dice distribution: 6dx3(3) cor averages 63 and clears flak, carapace, Sororitas and Astartes plate at 99%+, dropping to 36.3% against a Terminator. Against vehicles: AV10 99.0%, AV11 85.5%, AV12 36.3%, AV13 0.99%, AV14 0% — a real light-vehicle killer (a Rhino's side armour, AV11, goes down more often than not) and a serious personal- armour threat, matching \"shears through light vehicle armour as readily as flesh\" without claiming it cracks a main battle tank outright. The high point cost is deliberate: framework.md ranks lore accuracy over playability, and a bio-titan's own tank-cracking bite should cost accordingly, in the same spirit as this project's most expensive Necron relic weapons and Custodes packages.",
